Apply the same snapshot/qual check to growing candidates as to sealed ones.

The finite scan used to admit high-scoring growing rows before checking the
executor's snapshot or WHERE clause. Invisible and out-of-scope rows could
fill top-k and raise its pruning threshold, discarding valid sealed matches.
The backend's exact completion repaired the answer, but common terms then
scanned and sorted their entire posting lists. Keep the exact path as a
correctness fallback; do not create the avoidable short page in the first
place. Respect enable_prefilter=off, as the sealed scan already does.

